WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.735
Open the Cluster Storage Standard workflow after deployment.

00:00:03.883 --> 00:00:08.426
It runs separately and is not inserted automatically into a recovery pipeline.

00:00:08.486 --> 00:00:12.840
Supply exactly three distinct replacement-container
names and the settings intended

00:00:12.924 --> 00:00:16.574
for this cluster. Use a saved PE credential reference.

00:00:16.764 --> 00:00:20.104
PE certificate verification is optional per operation.

00:00:20.326 --> 00:00:24.530
An exception needs its reason and stays bound to the reviewed configuration and

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:28.904
approval. HTTPS remains encrypted, but certificate-based

00:00:28.944 --> 00:00:31.976
PE identity is not verified with an exception.

00:00:32.144 --> 00:00:34.114
Never put its password in YAML.

00:00:34.251 --> 00:00:36.962
Select Discover default, read-only.

00:00:37.238 --> 00:00:41.484
Review the cluster UUID and the exact default-container name and

00:00:41.504 --> 00:00:44.280
UUID captured into the configuration.

00:00:44.491 --> 00:00:48.989
The numeric suffix matters. Multiple candidates, unsupported inventories

00:00:49.158 --> 00:00:51.720
or an unexpected default name block review;

00:00:51.931 --> 00:00:55.005
the workflow does not guess which container can be removed.

00:00:55.387 --> 00:00:59.833
Review the replacements, settings and dependencies before requesting approval.

00:00:59.966 --> 00:01:03.765
A different administrator must approve the exact YAML and filename.

00:01:03.806 --> 00:01:06.432
Editing the file invalidates that approval.

00:01:06.622 --> 00:01:10.016
The operator confirmation binds submission to the reviewed cluster;

00:01:10.078 --> 00:01:13.058
a browser disconnect is not a reason to submit again.

00:01:13.338 --> 00:01:17.755
The worker verifies existing replacements
before creating missing ones, then reads

00:01:17.775 --> 00:01:21.105
back all three and checks the explicitly requested properties.

00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:25.084
Existing mismatches fail rather than being silently rewritten.

00:01:25.305 --> 00:01:29.723
Only the exact reviewed default is considered
for cleanup, and dependencies must

00:01:29.743 --> 00:01:31.337
pass the conservative checks.

00:01:31.662 --> 00:01:36.102
Retain the job and inspect actual storage state if creation, verification

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.703
or cleanup fails. A familiar name does not prove a container is empty

00:01:40.723 --> 00:01:45.120
or disposable. Complete the documented
storage and workload acceptance before

00:01:45.203 --> 00:01:46.912
using the result operationally.

00:01:47.038 --> 00:01:50.565
This walkthrough uses simulated inventory and deletes nothing.
